        "original_id": "0c081a5f-de92-5b4a-9738-5fbfbecb2902",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Wilm Hosenfeld, Władysław Szpilman\n- Places: Nazi-occupied Poland, Warsaw\n- Works: The Pianist\n- Topics: rescue of Jews during World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Władysław Szpilman was born on 5 December 1911 and died on 6 July 2000.\n- Władysław Szpilman was a Polish pianist and a classical composer of Jewish descent.\n- During Nazi-occupied Poland, Wilm Hosenfeld helped hide or rescue several Polish people, including Jews.\n- During the last months of 1944, in the ruins of Warsaw, Wilm Hosenfeld helped the Polish-Jewish pianist and composer Władysław Szpilman survive while in hiding.\n- Wilm Hosenfeld’s help to Władysław Szpilman was portrayed in the 2002 film The Pianist.",
